From 82efb224e1f1321e28aea748ff8cb8d8baffe21d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:15:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 105/114] core: answer the legacy provisioning API from the
 provision database

oFono 2.x replaced the gprs-provision plugin interface with a compiled
provision database. Plugins written against the old API, including
ofono-binder-plugin, still call ofono_gprs_provision_get_settings().

Reinstate that API as a thin adapter over __ofono_provision_get_settings()
so the access points a plugin looks up are answered from the new database.

provider_name is always NULL. The database stores access points but not
the operator's name: tools/provisiontool parses <provider><name> and then
discards it, and the binary format has no field for it. Carrying it would
mean changing the format and the generator. Callers already have to check
the field, and the binder driver only uses it to prettify an odd operator
name, so it falls back to the network-reported name.

Note that the generator maps authentication as chap=0, pap=1, none=2,
matching upstream's enum. This is why OFONO_GPRS_AUTH_METHOD_ANY was
appended rather than inserted in Sailfish's order: renumbering would have
silently misread every access point in the database.

(cherry picked from commit 773de93b044f0315c2e30bef0305642dfc1e72d8)
Upstream-Status: Pending
